program ProRock.Xmlite.DocumentPropertiesSample;

// The core properties of an Office document (.docx, .xlsx, .pptx): title, author, keywords... - the ones Office shows in
// File > Info - opened, edited and saved, and the application's own (docProps/app.xml: the sheet or slide titles) shown.
// The document is opened with ProRock.Office.Ooxml (OPC, Ecma-376 Part 2: the core properties on Dublin Core); app.xml is
// read with a unit generated by ProRocket from its official schema (Part 4: the extended properties). Every other part of
// the file is copied as it is. Usage: ProRock.Xmlite.DocumentPropertiesSample [<document>] - or open / drop a file in the
// window
//
// The schema notices are in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md (ECMA-376 Part 2, © Ecma International). Dublin Core:
